Live Link: https://licensedcare.vercel.app
Repo: https://github.com/JamesManon-og/LicensedCareMN

I worked through the README requirements, tested each existing feature, fixed the problems I found, and improved several parts of the app.

Some improvements:
- Fixed the database, login, admin, and provider access problems.
- Made provider search tolerate typos, and added search by license number and ZIP code.
- Made CSV importing safer, with validation and a preview before publishing.
- Required a confirmation, and a fresh re-check, before publishing can remove any providers.
- Got provider claims and owner editing working, and let admins revoke a claim.
- Made the site handle database and service failures clearly, instead of showing empty results.
- Added security checks for private features, login redirects, and provider website links.
- Made license numbers, addresses, services, cities, and counties clickable.
- Added automated tests for the main features and fixes.

In short: the README requirements work, the problems I found are fixed, and the improvements are covered by automated tests.
